                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Holobunnies: Pause Cafe is a quick little game but worth the money if you like challenging yourself.  While the content is limited the price point matches it well.\n\nThere are 3 different modes:\n\nBoss Rush - Quick boss battle timed rush mode.  Fight 4 different bosses with 4 different Holobunnies.  The first time I played this is took 10 minutes.  The second time took just under 6 minutes.\n\nKitcat's Adventure (Runner Mode) - An auto-runner style mode that pits your timing perfectly against the challenging environments.  Easily brings you back in to try and beat it and then make good on bettering your time each run as you memorize the levels and timed jumps.\n\nBrawler - Unfortunately my buddy and I had an issue with this mode.  We used controllers and everything went fine until  after we selected our characters.  Once we entered the battle arena only I could work my controller and oddly enough I controlled both characters simultaneously.  He couldn't do anything beyond pausing the game.  Not sure if this was an internal bug or if our controllers just started acting funny.  Further testing will be needed to decipher the cause of that bug.\n\nIn the end, Holobunnies: Pause Cafe is an enjoyable game with creative visuals and some replayability that should keep you going for a couple hours if you're the type that enjoys challenging themselves in time attack Boss Rush/Runner style games.",
